# Music library

Unity now plays menu, collection and selectable battle music from this library.
See [Unity audio controls](../../docs/unity-audio.md).

**21 downloaded tracks:** 19 Pokémon battle selections and two menu/deck-building
loops. All files passed full audio decoding and SHA-256 checks. Two existing result
cues are reused by reference from `assets/audio/`.

## Default soundtrack

| Game context | Track |
| --- | --- |
| Main menu | Menu Music — mrpoly |
| Deck builder and collection | Other Center — Chris Murphy (zesona) |
| Standard battle | HeartGold/SoulSilver Kanto trainer theme |
| Rival battle | Black 2/White 2 rival theme |
| Boss battle | Black 2/White 2 Kanto Gym Leader theme |
| Championship | Showdown's `spl-elite4` selection |
| Victory | Existing Kenney NES jingle (`jingles_NES00`) |
| Defeat | Existing short descending cue (`phaserDown3`) |

These are initial playlist choices. The battle folder also includes trainer/rival
alternatives from Diamond/Pearl/Platinum, Black/White, X/Y, Omega Ruby/Alpha Sapphire,
and Sun/Moon, plus Johto and Miror B. selections.
This is a selection from Pokémon Showdown's music library; the original Pokémon
TCG Game Boy soundtrack is not included.

## Files and integration

- `manifest.json`: tracks by ID, paths, hashes, durations, formats, source information,
  volume defaults, loop points and game contexts.
- `playlists.json`: convenient context-to-track mapping and alternatives.
- `catalog.csv`: portable music inventory.
- `verification.json`: decode, hash, loop-bound and playlist validation results.
- `source/`: original download records, saved author pages and pinned loop metadata.
- `previews/music-sampler.mp3`: menu, deck builder, Kanto battle — eight seconds each.

Paths are relative to this folder. `externalManifest` paths for result sounds are
also relative to this folder. Keep `assets/music/` and `assets/audio/` together.

Battle tracks contain an intro and repeated material. Play from zero the first time,
then repeat between `loop.startSeconds` and `loop.endSeconds`. These values come
from Pokémon Showdown's pinned playback source and have been checked against each
file's duration. The menu authors describe their tracks as whole-file loops; their
end points use the decoded track duration. Loop seams still need listening review.

For a future Web Audio player:

```js
// bufferSource.buffer must already contain the decoded selected track.
bufferSource.loop = track.loop.enabled;
bufferSource.loopStart = track.loop.startSeconds;
bufferSource.loopEnd = track.loop.endSeconds;
musicGain.gain.value = track.recommendedGain * userMusicVolume;
bufferSource.connect(musicGain);
bufferSource.start(0); // Run after a user gesture resumes the AudioContext.
```

Default music gain is 0.22. Source recordings are unchanged; only the sampler is
edited. Keep a separate music volume and mute control, crossfade when changing
tracks, and avoid restarting the battle track on every turn. Runtime music playback
and transitions are not implemented by this asset folder.

